{
  "requirement": "Evidence inputs MAY have a definition form containing exactly `definition` and `text`. `definition` MUST identify one named definition; `text` MUST contain its complete raw fenced declaration as source lines, including its phrase option and explanatory body.\n\nValidation MUST reject missing definitions and changed snapshot text, identifying the definition and showing a compact diff when available. Moving an unchanged definition within its chapter MUST NOT invalidate its snapshot. Evidence displays MUST show the definition name, current source location, and recorded text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: satisfied.** The implementation covers every obligation in `requirements.definitions.inputs`, and the tests cover the main boundaries and failure cases. I did not run the tests.\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Shape:** `validate_input` (src/evidence.rs) routes an object with a `definition` key to the definition form.\n  - `check_keys` allows only `definition` and `text` and rejects any other field. `tests/definitions.rs` exercises this with an `unexpected` field, which produces \"unexpected field\".\n  - `string_field` requires `definition` to be a string.\n  - `text_field` requires `text` to be a nonempty array of strings.\n- **Which definition:** `InputSelector::resolve` (src/inputs.rs) accepts only a `DefinitionKind::Term` entry. A name that is missing, or that names a requirement or example, fails with \"<name>: no matching named definition\". The error names the offending definition and the input label.\n- **Text:** the resolved text is `Declaration::raw_lines`. `collect_definitions` builds these as the raw fenced declaration, from the opening fence through the closing fence, with the option lines such as `:phrase:` kept in the body. Position is not part of the text, so moving a definition within its chapter leaves it unchanged.\n- **Changed snapshots:** `validate_resolved_input` compares the recorded text with the current text. On a difference it reports \"input text changed for Definition { definition: … }\" followed by `compact_diff`.\n- **Recording and matching:** `InputSelector::to_input` records the `{definition, text}` form, and `from_input` recognises it when matching existing inputs.\n- **Display:** in src/index.rs, `InputLocation::resolve` and `render_input` show `definition <name>`, then the current source location from the resolved range (name plus file and line range), then the recorded `text`. If the selector no longer resolves, the page reports \"Unresolved selector\" and keeps the recorded text.\n- **Marking:** all of these functions carry `{impl}` references to this requirement.\n\n**Tests**\n- `changed_definition_snapshots_show_a_compact_diff_and_text_is_required` (tests/definitions.rs):\n  - A change to a body line makes validation report \"input text changed\" for `glossary.a`, and the diff is exactly the `-`/`+` pair for the changed line.\n  - Missing `text`, an empty `text` array and a non-array `text` are each rejected.\n- `cyclic_dependencies_are_captured_once_and_changes_require_review` (tests/definitions.rs):\n  - Prepending blank lines to the glossary, which moves the definitions, produces no errors.\n  - Changing the `:phrase:` option or the body text is flagged.\n  - A removed or duplicated definition input is flagged.\n- `definition_schema_deletion_and_literal_references_are_checked` (tests/definitions.rs): an unexpected field is rejected, and deleting the glossary file gives \"glossary.a … no matching named definition\".\n- `detail_page_shows_recorded_text_locations_and_first_matching_group` (src/index.rs): the definition input shows its name, its `md/rules.md:9–13` location and its recorded text, in that order. The unresolved-selector case keeps the recorded text.\n\n**Gaps**\nNone found. No behaviour in the `{impl}` code goes beyond what this requirement or another cited requirement specifies. The 8-line diff truncation belongs to `requirements.ci.diagnostics` and is tested there.",
  "references": "5f27461ed46183dca8e240ed4e7780d7ea9614bfaabbece36921a4b4d7fbba30",
